   $q$Which revision of sentence 10 best explains how the evidence in sentences 7 and 9 supports the writer's analysis?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The bell is the most important object in the story, and readers should pay close attention to it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-explanation"},{"text":"Marisol rang the bell twice, slowly, after the last runner from the bakery reached the ramp before the crossing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-analysis"},{"text":"By waiting for the late runner and ringing so everyone can hear, Marisol shows she now sees the bell as a duty to every passenger.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Marisol will probably take over the ferry for good and run it for the rest of her life.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By waiting for the late runner and ringing so everyone can hear, Marisol shows she now sees the bell as a duty to every passenger.$q$, $q$The first choice explains what the waiting and the slow ringing reveal about Marisol's new sense of responsibility. The second choice only retells the events in sentence 7 without saying what they show.$q$, 'draft', '57329ddd-a95d-5346-b2ef-98b651da1a8b')
