   $q$How should the writer handle the limitation in sentence 10?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Keep it, and conclude that the screens probably had no effect on ridership at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overcorrects"},{"text":"Keep it, and point out that the survey about how waits felt still supports the claim even if busy stops grew faster.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Delete it, because mentioning any weakness in a source makes the whole response less convincing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"hides-counterevidence"},{"text":"Move it to the first sentence of the draft so that readers see the problem right away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reorder-not-explain"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Keep it, and point out that the survey about how waits felt still supports the claim even if busy stops grew faster.$q$, $q$The limitation weakens only the boarding numbers, while the survey evidence in sentences 3 and 4 is untouched, so the writer can acknowledge it and lean on the stronger evidence. Deleting it would hide a point Haddad herself admits.$q$, 'draft', '552c5a16-ea51-552f-9486-690415890400')
