   $q$How does the second paragraph (sentences 8 to 10) strengthen the writer's claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Castellanos disagrees with Bello about how to use the diaries.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that Ferrante's diaries are full of errors and should not be used by scientists at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overcorrects"},{"text":"It shows that Ferrante's students were better at taking readings than she was.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-evidence"},{"text":"It shows that testing caught and removed weaker readings, supporting the idea that records become useful once they are checked.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that testing caught and removed weaker readings, supporting the idea that records become useful once they are checked.$q$, $q$The claim says amateur records become valuable when tested, and paragraph 2 shows that testing in action: weak weeks were found and removed. The draft says the students' weeks had more errors, so they were not better at it.$q$, 'draft', 'e30d68c0-c979-5c17-a80e-dae56e7cea1f')
