  ('a2a71f54-9583-5667-b097-c301e6d1d140', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The writer wants to add this quotation after sentence 7: the ice record "turns a teacher's habit into a measuring stick for a changing lake." Which version integrates it most smoothly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Castellanos says that \"turns a teacher's habit into a measuring stick for a changing lake.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"grammar-mismatch"},{"text":"\"Turns a teacher's habit into a measuring stick for a changing lake.\" This is from the article.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dropped-quotation"},{"text":"Castellanos sums up the value of this work when she writes that the ice record \"turns a teacher's habit into a measuring stick for a changing lake.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"Ferrante wrote in her diary that the ice record \"turns a teacher's habit into a measuring stick for a changing lake.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misattributed-quotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Castellanos sums up the value of this work when she writes that the ice record "turns a teacher's habit into a measuring stick for a changing lake."$q$, $q$The first choice names Castellanos as the source and builds the quotation into a complete, grammatical sentence. The version beginning "Castellanos says that" leaves the quoted phrase without a subject, so the sentence does not work.$q$, 'draft', 'e30d68c0-c979-5c17-a80e-dae56e7cea1f')
